 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Family",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "One part in three temperature grades: ST485EC for 0 to 70 °C, ST485EB for -40 to 85 °C and ST485EX for -55 to 125 °C. Each pairs a single driver with a single receiver, joined on the A/B pair for half-duplex links, runs from one 5 V supply and comes in SO-8. The EB grade ships in tubes or on reels, the EC and EX grades on reels of 2500."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Driver",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With DE high the driver follows DI: A takes DI's level and B the opposite. With DE low both outputs are in high impedance, and they stay so with the supply removed. Loaded with 27 Ω (RS-485) or 50 Ω (RS-422) the differential output is at least 1.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Receiver",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With RE low, RO is high when A exceeds B by 0.2 V or more and low when B exceeds A by 0.2 V or more, over a common-mode range of -7 V to 12 V. Receiver input hysteresis is 70 mV typical at 0 V common mode. With A and B left open RO reads high. RE high puts RO in high impedance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bus loading",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Receiver input resistance is 96 kΩ minimum across the -7 V to 12 V common-mode range. Up to 256 transceivers can share one bus. Bus pin current with the driver off is at most 1 mA at 12 V and -0.8 mA at -7 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Driver output current is limited, at 35 mA to 250 mA peak into a short anywhere from -7 V to 12 V. If dissipation becomes excessive, a thermal shutdown puts the driver outputs into high impedance. The bus pins are protected to ±15 kV (human body model) and ±8 kV (IEC-1000-4-2, contact discharge) without latch-up."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply current",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Unloaded, the part draws 300 µA typical (500 µA max) with the driver disabled and 400 µA typical (900 µA max) with it enabled. The disabled-driver figure holds also when the bus is loaded. Typical supply current falls with temperature, from about 420 µA at -50 °C to about 343 µA at 125 °C with DE high."
  }
 ],
